    "BrochureContent": [
      {
        "ContentType": "Description",
        "SortOrder": 0,
        "Content": "Niall Browne & Co is delighted to bring No. 61 Rosán Glas to the market, a four-bedroom home arranged over three floors in this popular and well-established residential development off Rahoon Road, Rahoon Hill. Extending to approximately 119 sq m (1,281 sq ft), the accommodation comprises an entrance hallway, living room, dining room and kitchen at ground floor level, three bedrooms and a family bathroom to the first floor, and a further bedroom and bathroom on the converted second floor, giving genuine flexibility for a growing family, a home office, or guest accommodation.\r\n\r\nThe living room retains a feature fireplace and looks out over the front of the development, while the kitchen/dining area opens onto a good-sized rear garden that offers real scope for the next owner to put their own stamp on it. Timber flooring runs throughout much of the house, and the second-floor bedroom benefits from its own bathroom, along with attractive dormer windows that bring in plenty of natural light.\r\n\r\nRosán Glas sits on Rahoon Hill, just off Rahoon Road, bordering Knocknacarra and within easy reach of Salthill and Galway city centre. Dunnes Stores, the Knocknacarra shopping area and the Gateway Retail Park are close by, as are Gaelscoil Mhic Amhlaigh and St John the Apostle Knocknacarra National School. Bus routes 411, 412 and 405 serve the immediate area, providing regular links to the city centre, the University of Galway and University Hospital Galway.\r\n\r\nProperties of this size in this development are consistently popular, and viewing is highly advised and recommended."
      }
    ],
